# Expected Nushell Grammar

It is a target grammar for a Nushell parser, based on the official Nushell book and the
syntax already represented in this repository's parser and tests.

Notation: terminals are quoted, token names are uppercase, `?` means optional,
`*` means zero or more, and `+` means one or more.

## Program, Blocks, and Pipelines

program        → shebang? block EOF ;
shebang        → "#!" any_until_newline NEWLINE ;

block          → block_item ( terminator+ block_item )* terminator* ;
block_item     → declaration
               | loop_statement
               | flow_statement
               | assignment
               | pipeline ;
terminator     → NEWLINE | ";" ;

pipeline       → pipe_element ( pipe pipe_element )* ;
pipe_element   → expression_command redirection* ;
pipe           → "|"
               | "err>|" | "e>|"
               | "out+err>|" | "err+out>|" | "o+e>|" | "e+o>|" ;

redirection    → file_redirection expression ;
file_redirection
               → "out>" | "o>" | "out>>" | "o>>"
               | "err>" | "e>" | "err>>" | "e>>"
               | "out+err>" | "err+out>" | "o+e>" | "e+o>"
               | "out+err>>" | "err+out>>" | "o+e>>" | "e+o>>" ;

## Declarations and Statements

declaration    → let_decl
               | mut_decl
               | const_decl
               | def_decl
               | extern_decl
               | alias_decl
               | module_decl
               | use_decl
               | source_decl
               | export_decl
               | export_env_decl
               | hide_decl
               | overlay_decl
               | plugin_use_decl ;

let_decl       → "let" binding "=" pipeline ;
mut_decl       → "mut" binding "=" pipeline ;
const_decl     → "const" binding "=" expression ;
binding        → variable_decl type_annotation? ;
variable_decl  → IDENTIFIER
               | "$" IDENTIFIER ;

def_decl       → "def" def_option* command_name type_params? signature io_signature? block_literal ;
def_option     → "--env" | "--wrapped" ;

extern_decl    → "extern" command_name signature ;
alias_decl     → "alias" command_name "=" pipeline ;

module_decl    → "module" module_name block_literal
               | "module" module_path ;
use_decl       → "use" import_pattern ;
source_decl    → "source" expression
               | "source-env" expression ;

export_decl    → "export" exportable_declaration ;
exportable_declaration
               → def_decl
               | extern_decl
               | alias_decl
               | const_decl
               | module_decl
               | use_decl ;
export_env_decl
               → "export-env" block_literal ;

hide_decl      → "hide" import_pattern ;
overlay_decl   → "overlay" overlay_action ;
overlay_action → "use" overlay_use_flag* import_pattern overlay_rename?
               | "hide" overlay_hide_flag* command_name? overlay_hide_flag*
               | "new" command_name
               | "list" ;
overlay_use_flag
               → "--prefix" ;
overlay_rename → "as" command_name ;
overlay_hide_flag
               → "--keep-custom"
               | "--keep-env" list ;
plugin_use_decl
               → "plugin" "use" expression ;

assignment     → cell_ref assign_op pipeline ;
assign_op      → "=" | "+=" | "-=" | "*=" | "/=" | "++=" ;

loop_statement → for_statement
               | while_statement
               | loop_forever ;
for_statement  → "for" variable_decl "in" expression block_literal ;
while_statement
               → "while" expression block_literal ;
loop_forever   → "loop" block_literal ;

flow_statement → return_statement
               | break_statement
               | continue_statement ;
return_statement
               → "return" expression? ;
break_statement
               → "break" ;
continue_statement
               → "continue" ;

## Commands and Arguments

expression_command
               → env_shorthand* command ;
env_shorthand  → ENV_NAME "=" ( STRING | variable | bare_word ) ;

command        → external_call
               | internal_call
               | expression ;
external_call  → "^" external_name external_arg* ;
external_name  → command_name
               | variable
               | STRING ;
external_arg   → spread
               | expression
               | bare_word
               | STRING ;

internal_call  → command_name argument* ;
command_name   → command_part+
               | STRING ;
command_part   → IDENTIFIER ;
argument       → flag
               | spread
               | expression
               | bare_word ;
flag           → "--" FLAG_NAME ( "=" expression | expression )?
               | "-" SHORT_FLAGS ( "=" expression | expression )? ;
spread         → "..." expression ;

## Expressions

expression     → logical_or ;

logical_or     → logical_xor ( "or" logical_xor )* ;
logical_xor    → logical_and ( "xor" logical_and )* ;
logical_and    → bit_or ( "and" bit_or )* ;
bit_or         → bit_xor ( "bit-or" bit_xor )* ;
bit_xor        → bit_and ( "bit-xor" bit_and )* ;
bit_and        → comparison ( "bit-and" comparison )* ;
comparison     → shift ( comparison_op shift )* ;
comparison_op  → "==" | "!=" | "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">="
               | "=~" | "!~" | "like" | "not-like"
               | "in" | "not-in"
               | "has" | "not-has"
               | "starts-with" | "not-starts-with"
               | "ends-with" | "not-ends-with"
               | "++" ;
shift          → term ( ( "bit-shl" | "bit-shr" ) term )* ;
term           → factor ( ( "+" | "-" ) factor )* ;
factor         → power ( ( "*" | "/" | "//" | "mod" ) power )* ;
power          → unary ( "**" power )? ;
unary          → ( "not" | "+" | "-" ) unary
               | postfix ;
postfix        → primary cell_path? ;

primary        → literal
               | variable
               | cell_path_literal
               | list
               | table
               | record
               | closure
               | block_literal
               | subexpression
               | range
               | if_expr
               | try_expr
               | match_expr ;

literal        → INT | FLOAT | FILESIZE | DURATION | DATE
               | STRING | RAW_STRING | INTERPOLATED_STRING | BACKTICK_STRING
               | BINARY | BOOL | "null" ;

variable       → "$" IDENTIFIER
               | "$in" | "$it" | "$env" | "$nu"
               | "$NU_LIB_DIRS" | "$NU_PLUGIN_DIRS" ;

cell_ref       → variable cell_path?
               | cell_path_literal ;
cell_path_literal
               → "$" cell_path ;
cell_path      → cell_member+ ;
cell_member    → "." path_member "?"? ;
path_member    → IDENTIFIER
               | INT
               | STRING ;

subexpression  → "(" block ")" ;
block_literal  → "{" block "}" ;

range          → range_bound? range_op range_bound?
               | range_bound ".." range_bound range_op range_bound ;
range_op       → ".." | "..<" ;
range_bound    → postfix ;

## Collection Literals

list           → "[" list_items? "]" ;
list_items     → list_item ( separator? list_item )* separator? ;
list_item      → spread
               | expression
               | bare_word ;

table          → "[" table_header ";" table_row* "]" ;
table_header   → "[" table_header_names? "]" ;
table_header_names
               → table_header_name ( separator? table_header_name )* separator? ;
table_header_name
               → IDENTIFIER | STRING ;
table_row      → "[" table_row_values? "]" separator? ;
table_row_values
               → table_row_value ( separator? table_row_value )* separator? ;
table_row_value
               → expression | bare_word ;

record         → "{" record_items? "}" ;
record_items   → record_item ( separator? record_item )* separator? ;
record_item    → record_key ":" expression ;
record_key     → IDENTIFIER
               | STRING ;

closure        → "{||" block "}"
               | "{|" closure_param_list? "|" block "}"
               | "{" block "}" ;
closure_param_list
               → closure_param ( "," closure_param )* ","? ;
closure_param  → IDENTIFIER type_annotation? ;

separator      → "," | NEWLINE | ";" ;

## Control Expressions

if_expr        → "if" expression block_literal else_clause? ;
else_clause    → "else" ( if_expr | match_expr | block_literal ) ;

try_expr       → "try" block_literal catch_clause? finally_clause? ;
catch_clause   → "catch" ( closure | block_literal ) ;
finally_clause → "finally" block_literal ;

match_expr     → "match" expression match_block ;
match_block    → "{" match_arm ( separator match_arm )* separator? "}" ;
match_arm      → pattern guard? "=>" ( expression | block_literal ) ;
guard          → "if" expression ;

pattern        → or_pattern ;
or_pattern     → single_pattern ( "|" single_pattern )* ;
single_pattern → "_"
               | literal
               | variable
               | list_pattern
               | record_pattern ;
list_pattern   → "[" pattern ( "," pattern )* ","? "]" ;
record_pattern → "{" record_pattern_item ( "," record_pattern_item )* ","? "}" ;
record_pattern_item
               → record_key ":" pattern ;

## Signatures and Types

signature      → "[" signature_param ( separator? signature_param )* separator? "]" ;
signature_param
               → positional_param
               | rest_param
               | flag_param
               | short_only_flag ;

positional_param
               → IDENTIFIER "?"? type_annotation? default_value? ;
rest_param     → "..." IDENTIFIER type_annotation? ;
flag_param     → "--" FLAG_NAME short_flag? type_annotation? default_value? ;
short_only_flag
               → "-" SHORT_FLAGS type_annotation? default_value? ;
short_flag     → "(" "-" SHORT_FLAGS ")" ;
default_value  → "=" expression ;

io_signature   → ":" in_out_type
               | ":" "[" in_out_type ( separator? in_out_type )* separator? "]" ;
in_out_type    → type "->" type ;

type_annotation
               → ":" type completer? ;
completer      → "@" command_name ;

type_params    → "<" IDENTIFIER ( "," IDENTIFIER )* ","? ">" ;
type           → IDENTIFIER type_args? "?"?
               | "record" "<" record_type_fields? ">" "?"? ;
type_args      → "<" type ( "," type )* ","? ">" ;
record_type_fields
               → record_type_field ( "," record_type_field )* ","? ;
record_type_field
               → record_key type_annotation? ;

## Imports and Modules

import_pattern → module_ref import_members? ;
module_ref     → module_path
               | module_name ;
import_members → "*"
               | command_name
               | "[" import_member_list? "]" ;
import_member_list
               → import_member ( separator? import_member )* separator? ;
import_member  → command_name
               | STRING
               | "*" ;

module_name    → command_name
               | STRING ;
module_path    → PATH
               | STRING ;

## Lexical Grammar

COMMENT        → "#" any_until_newline ;
NEWLINE        → "\n" | "\r\n" | "\x0C" ;
INT            → sign? decimal_int
               | sign? "0x" hex_digit+
               | sign? "0o" oct_digit+
               | sign? "0b" bin_digit+ ;
FLOAT          → sign? decimal_int? "." digit+ exponent?
               | sign? decimal_int "." digit* exponent?
               | "Infinity" | "-Infinity" | "NaN" ;
FILESIZE       → number filesize_unit ;
DURATION       → number duration_unit ;
DATE           → yyyy "-" mm "-" dd time_and_zone? ;
BINARY         → "0x[" hex_pair* "]"
               | "0o[" oct_digit* "]"
               | "0b[" bin_digit* "]" ;
BOOL           → "true" | "false" ;

STRING         → SINGLE_QUOTED_STRING
               | DOUBLE_QUOTED_STRING
               | BACKTICK_STRING ;
RAW_STRING     → "r" "#"+ "'" raw_contents "'" "#"+ ;
INTERPOLATED_STRING
               → "$\"" interpolation_part* "\""
               | "$'" interpolation_part* "'" ;
interpolation_part
               → string_chunk
               | "(" block ")" ;

bare_word      → BARE ;
BARE           → unquoted_word_char+ ;
IDENTIFIER     → BARE ;
ENV_NAME       → IDENTIFIER ;
FLAG_NAME      → IDENTIFIER ( "-" IDENTIFIER )* ;
SHORT_FLAGS    → IDENTIFIER ;

## Disambiguation Rules

Bare words have context-sensitive meaning:

bare_word      → STRING in value positions such as list items, record values, and command arguments ;
bare_word      → command_name in command head position ;

Command names are recognized at parse time. A quoted string can define or call a command name
that contains spaces; an unquoted multi-word command name is parsed as command name parts until
the first argument boundary.

Operators used as infix expressions must be tokenized as operators, not as bare command
arguments. In parser implementations that preserve Nushell's whitespace rule, infix operators
should have horizontal whitespace around them.

Statements such as `for`, `while`, `loop`, `return`, `break`, and `continue` are block items.
They are not valid as middle elements of an output-producing pipeline.

Variable names are bare identifiers after `$`. Nushell variable names do not include structural
or operator characters such as `.`, `[`, `(`, `{`, `+`, `-`, `*`, `^`, `/`, `=`, `!`, `<`, `>`,
`&`, or `|`.

